flowchart TB
    Internet((Internet))
    Admin[Admin Browser]
    Sender[External SMTP]
    Customer[Customer Mail Server]

    subgraph Public["Public Edge"]
        ALB[ALB + WAF\n443]
        MX1[Dedicated Postfix EC2\nmx1 :25]
        MX2[Dedicated Postfix EC2\nmx2 :25]
        Relay[Outbound/Relay Postfix\ncommissioned EIP]
    end

    subgraph App["Private Application / ECS"]
        Frontend[Frontend]
        Control[Control Backend / BFF]
        Workers[Async Workers]
        Scanners[Scanner ECS/EC2 Capacity]
    end

    subgraph Data["Private Data / Security"]
        PG[(PostgreSQL)]
        Redis[(Redis / Valkey)]
        S3[(S3 via private path)]
        Bao[OpenBao]
        IDP[ZITADEL]
        SQS[(SQS)]
    end

    subgraph AI["Private AI"]
        AIAPI[Authenticated Deep AI Endpoint]
        GPU[Accelerated EC2 / ECS Capacity]
    end

    Admin -->|443| ALB
    ALB --> Frontend
    ALB --> Control

    Sender -->|25| MX1
    Sender -->|25| MX2
    Customer -->|25/587 when explicitly enabled| Relay

    MX1 --> Scanners
    MX2 --> Scanners
    Relay --> Scanners

    Control --> PG
    Control --> Redis
    Control --> S3
    Control --> Bao
    Control --> IDP
    Workers --> SQS
    Scanners --> S3
    Scanners --> Redis
    Scanners --> AIAPI --> GPU

    Relay -->|25 direct MX using stable EIP/PTR| Internet

    Note1[Security Groups: deny by absence; SG-to-SG private access]
    Note2[No public SSH / DB / cache / secrets / scanner / AI]
    Note3[ECS baseline; dedicated mail EC2 is intentional exception]

    App -.-> Note1
    Data -.-> Note2
    Public -.-> Note3
